Copied/adapted from packages/coding-agent/src/web/search/:
- query.ts and utils.ts
- providers/brave.ts, tavily.ts, jina.ts, synthetic.ts, ollama.ts,
  tinyfish.ts, duckduckgo.ts, utils.ts, kimi.ts, zai.ts,
  startpage.ts, google.ts, ecosia.ts, mojeek.ts
- Perplexity consumer SSE parser/transport from providers/perplexity.ts
- Query tests from packages/coding-agent/test/web/search/query.test.ts

Reimplemented from the same source tree's index.ts, types.ts,
providers/base.ts, providers/parallel.ts, and providers/exa.ts:
- Standalone provider contract and Pi tool registration
- Parallel/Exa REST and public MCP adapters
- Result formatting and sequential fallback

Local changes replace OMP/Bun APIs with Node fetch, a small injectable
API-key adapter, bounded transport, TypeBox, and the Pi extension API.
Additional adapted protocol implementations:
- providers/anthropic.ts, gemini.ts, codex.ts, xai.ts, openrouter.ts,
  perplexity-auth.ts, firecrawl.ts, searxng.ts, public.ts
- packages/coding-agent/src/web/kagi.ts
- packages/ai/src/registry/oauth/perplexity.ts, google-gemini-cli.ts,
  google-antigravity.ts, and catalog auth/*.kdl public OAuth client config
- packages/coding-agent/src/utils/browser-session.ts

The OMP SQLite/model catalog/browser broker runtime is not included.
OAuth flows are adapted to Pi's provider auth storage and refresh lifecycle.
See PORTING.md for platform differences and remaining parity gaps.
